1
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:12,680
(11:50-12:00 PM)

2
00:00:12,680 --> 00:00:19,200
(11:50-12:00 PM)

3
00:00:20,693 --> 00:00:23,773
♪Your silhouette melts into the glow♪

4
00:00:25,006 --> 00:00:26,679
(Congrats to our grand prize winner!
Prize money: 100,000 yuan)

5
00:00:27,127 --> 00:00:31,037
♪I count your sighs♪

6
00:00:32,622 --> 00:00:34,663
♪Every breath♪

7
00:00:34,946 --> 00:00:37,606
♪Feels like I'm stealing♪

8
00:00:39,927 --> 00:00:41,142
♪The next second♪

9
00:00:41,659 --> 00:00:44,513
♪Before it's no longer mine♪

10
00:00:48,054 --> 00:00:50,341
♪We live♪
(Capernaum)

11
00:00:50,342 --> 00:00:54,263
♪In the spaces between moments♪

12
00:00:56,241 --> 00:01:00,776
♪Breathing through each other's shadows♪

13
00:01:02,059 --> 00:01:05,010
♪Let's not speak of what's to come♪

14
00:01:05,353 --> 00:01:08,158
♪Or what came before♪

15
00:01:09,778 --> 00:01:14,486
♪This moment could last me a lifetime♪
(12:00-11:50 PM)

16
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:20,925
=Thirteen Types of Love=
=Episode 8=

17
00:01:24,840 --> 00:01:25,360
Night Owl.

18
00:01:43,040 --> 00:01:43,560
The code word.

19
00:01:46,360 --> 00:01:46,880
Are you nuts?

20
00:01:48,360 --> 00:01:49,320
I brought you breakfast.

21
00:01:49,560 --> 00:01:50,360
Hope you like it.

22
00:01:52,760 --> 00:01:53,440
Thanks.

23
00:01:57,400 --> 00:01:58,520
This is breakfast?

24
00:02:00,880 --> 00:02:02,120
What would you rather have?

25
00:02:03,120 --> 00:02:03,800
You're sick.

26
00:02:06,720 --> 00:02:08,520
Heath Ledger Kn1u2.

27
00:02:08,840 --> 00:02:10,800
Twisted connective tissue syndrome.

28
00:02:16,360 --> 00:02:16,840
What?

29
00:02:17,840 --> 00:02:19,360
The longer the name, the sooner you die?

30
00:02:21,200 --> 00:02:22,840
Good thing you didn't answer seriously,

31
00:02:23,080 --> 00:02:24,000
or I'd have shot you.

32
00:02:31,120 --> 00:02:32,840
Trackers. Locators.

33
00:02:33,160 --> 00:02:34,280
Smoke bombs. Poison darts.

34
00:02:34,480 --> 00:02:35,320
I got everything ready for you.

35
00:02:35,680 --> 00:02:36,080
Here.

36
00:02:37,200 --> 00:02:37,600
Take a look.

37
00:02:51,920 --> 00:02:52,880
Why isn't she dead yet?

38
00:02:54,360 --> 00:02:55,760
Did you betray the organization?

39
00:03:10,080 --> 00:03:11,440
One second, I trusted you.

40
00:03:11,920 --> 00:03:13,760
The next, you called in backup.

41
00:03:15,640 --> 00:03:16,680
Everybody, calm down.

42
00:03:17,200 --> 00:03:19,080
Can we talk instead of fighting?

43
00:03:19,960 --> 00:03:21,720
When we were cleaning up the scene
yesterday,

44
00:03:21,720 --> 00:03:23,360
we found our people zipped in body bags.

45
00:03:24,200 --> 00:03:25,360
Three of theirs died. Two were hurt.

46
00:03:25,360 --> 00:03:26,920
When you didn't show, we thought
something had happened to you.

47
00:03:28,320 --> 00:03:28,960
Well, that...

48
00:03:28,960 --> 00:03:30,480
It's a little complicated.

49
00:03:30,840 --> 00:03:31,560
Can we sit down

50
00:03:31,680 --> 00:03:32,840
and talk over coffee?

51
00:03:33,160 --> 00:03:34,320
I haven't even had breakfast.

52
00:03:36,520 --> 00:03:37,440
What a joke.

53
00:03:37,880 --> 00:03:39,200
I was actually starting to trust you.

54
00:03:40,160 --> 00:03:41,160
You planned this together?

55
00:03:44,360 --> 00:03:45,600
You planned this together?

56
00:03:48,080 --> 00:03:49,800
We won't get anywhere like this.

57
00:03:50,560 --> 00:03:51,760
Just give me a chance.

58
00:03:53,040 --> 00:03:54,520
Give you a chance?

59
00:03:55,360 --> 00:03:56,640
A chance?

60
00:04:00,480 --> 00:04:02,800
Give me a chance.

61
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:09,840
So you're saying

62
00:04:10,280 --> 00:04:11,760
our organizations have no reason

63
00:04:11,760 --> 00:04:12,880
to target each other.

64
00:04:15,520 --> 00:04:17,360
Someone must've stolen our intel

65
00:04:17,600 --> 00:04:18,880
and set us against each other,

66
00:04:19,080 --> 00:04:20,120
so they could swoop in
and take advantage.

67
00:04:21,560 --> 00:04:22,840
Is everything in this universe

68
00:04:23,360 --> 00:04:24,560
straight out of a TV drama?

69
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:31,880
Hitmen always have clients.

70
00:04:32,280 --> 00:04:33,840
There's no need to steal contracts.

71
00:04:34,400 --> 00:04:35,640
Each job pays well enough

72
00:04:35,720 --> 00:04:37,560
that one more or less

73
00:04:37,720 --> 00:04:38,640
isn't worth killing over.

74
00:04:39,120 --> 00:04:40,400
Then why break

75
00:04:40,560 --> 00:04:42,000
a balance that's lasted for years?

76
00:04:42,160 --> 00:04:43,840
Why would anyone want Coke and Pepsi

77
00:04:43,960 --> 00:04:45,120
both wiped off

78
00:04:45,240 --> 00:04:46,080
the face of the earth?

79
00:04:46,280 --> 00:04:47,720
Because another soda brand

80
00:04:47,720 --> 00:04:49,200
wants to take over the market.

81
00:04:51,080 --> 00:04:51,680
Who would that be?

82
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:52,560
No idea.

83
00:04:52,760 --> 00:04:53,360
No idea.

84
00:04:53,600 --> 00:04:54,280
No idea?

85
00:04:58,240 --> 00:04:59,080
Yongsen,

86
00:04:59,400 --> 00:05:00,000
read the messages.

87
00:05:00,160 --> 00:05:00,640
Monica,

88
00:05:01,160 --> 00:05:01,800
read the messages.

89
00:05:02,400 --> 00:05:03,920
(Camellia confirmed dead.
An Zu confirmed dead.)

90
00:05:04,040 --> 00:05:06,320
(Meet at the abandoned glass factory.)

91
00:05:06,480 --> 00:05:08,000
(Bring Night Owl's head.
Bring Bloody Rose's head.)

92
00:05:08,640 --> 00:05:09,160
It's her.

93
00:05:10,720 --> 00:05:12,080
You're jumping to conclusions.

94
00:05:12,600 --> 00:05:13,800
These messages don't even name anyone.

95
00:05:14,040 --> 00:05:15,320
That means each organization

96
00:05:15,440 --> 00:05:16,880
has a traitor inside.

97
00:05:17,120 --> 00:05:18,320
The messages don't address anyone.

98
00:05:18,680 --> 00:05:19,840
They could've been sent to everyone.

99
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:21,480
Exactly. No names.

100
00:05:22,360 --> 00:05:23,520
What... what names?

101
00:05:23,920 --> 00:05:25,720
Reply, and they can trace your location

102
00:05:25,880 --> 00:05:26,720
and wipe you out.

103
00:05:27,080 --> 00:05:27,720
Why?

104
00:05:28,400 --> 00:05:29,760
Camellia. Factory.

105
00:05:30,640 --> 00:05:31,120
Night Owl.

106
00:05:31,560 --> 00:05:32,920
An Zu. Factory.

107
00:05:33,520 --> 00:05:34,480
Bloody Rose.

108
00:05:34,880 --> 00:05:36,880
Nobody knows if Camellia's alive.

109
00:05:36,880 --> 00:05:37,640
Even if she's dead,

110
00:05:37,640 --> 00:05:39,040
it wouldn't cause a stir at the factory.

111
00:05:39,160 --> 00:05:41,360
The glass factory
offers plenty of cover.

112
00:05:41,520 --> 00:05:44,400
As for Night Owl and Bloody Rose...

113
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:46,160
Nobody knows you've spent

114
00:05:46,160 --> 00:05:47,240
all this time with Night Owl,

115
00:05:47,320 --> 00:05:48,800
or whether you died or I did.

116
00:05:48,920 --> 00:05:50,560
The messages are a test.

117
00:05:50,720 --> 00:05:52,400
No reply means you're dead.

118
00:05:52,480 --> 00:05:54,320
I take your head to An Zu.

119
00:05:54,520 --> 00:05:55,640
A reply means you're dead.

120
00:05:55,920 --> 00:05:57,600
I take your head to Camellia.

121
00:06:00,040 --> 00:06:00,520
Wait. Hold on.

122
00:06:00,840 --> 00:06:02,400
But your Cami-whatsit

123
00:06:02,400 --> 00:06:03,680
and your An-whatsit...

124
00:06:03,680 --> 00:06:04,320
Aren't they both dead?

125
00:06:04,440 --> 00:06:06,040
So do we reply or not?

126
00:06:06,160 --> 00:06:08,360
Depends who we decide to kill next.

127
00:06:10,160 --> 00:06:10,680
You die.

128
00:06:11,160 --> 00:06:11,640
You die.

129
00:06:12,640 --> 00:06:13,240
I die.

130
00:06:14,840 --> 00:06:15,760
Actually, I'll stay alive for now.

131
00:06:16,240 --> 00:06:17,040
This is way too confusing.

132
00:06:17,520 --> 00:06:18,720
I didn't understand a word.

133
00:06:19,280 --> 00:06:20,640
Say six people share a dorm room.

134
00:06:20,720 --> 00:06:21,920
One day, your phone goes missing.

135
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:23,360
Your five roommates are worried,

136
00:06:23,560 --> 00:06:24,880
so they all call to find it.

137
00:06:25,120 --> 00:06:26,520
But your phone's off,

138
00:06:26,720 --> 00:06:27,560
so you miss their calls.

139
00:06:27,840 --> 00:06:29,800
Then you finally find your phone.

140
00:06:29,920 --> 00:06:31,280
You turn it on and see missed calls

141
00:06:31,400 --> 00:06:31,960
and a bunch of messages.

142
00:06:32,040 --> 00:06:33,240
Before you can read them all,

143
00:06:33,320 --> 00:06:34,280
one of those five roommates

144
00:06:34,320 --> 00:06:35,240
calls you and says,

145
00:06:35,400 --> 00:06:36,360
"What? You found your phone?"

146
00:06:36,440 --> 00:06:37,080
"Where was it?"

147
00:06:37,160 --> 00:06:38,960
Who do you think stole your phone?

148
00:06:39,200 --> 00:06:39,760
Who did?

149
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:40,760
That guy.

150
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:41,600
Which guy?

151
00:06:41,680 --> 00:06:42,880
The one who called you.

152
00:06:43,080 --> 00:06:44,000
But who is that?

153
00:06:44,200 --> 00:06:45,280
The person behind those messages

154
00:06:45,360 --> 00:06:47,240
is the third brand trying to break in.

155
00:06:47,480 --> 00:06:48,360
One or two people alone

156
00:06:48,480 --> 00:06:49,880
couldn't pull off something this big.

157
00:06:50,080 --> 00:06:51,360
The messages just connect the dots.

158
00:06:51,960 --> 00:06:54,040
Someone else wants both sides gone.

159
00:06:54,280 --> 00:06:55,000
Find Equinox,

160
00:06:55,120 --> 00:06:56,000
and we'll find who's behind it.

161
00:06:56,520 --> 00:06:57,800
Find them, and then what?

162
00:06:58,040 --> 00:06:59,640
Eliminate them, or we're dead.

163
00:07:04,080 --> 00:07:05,880
Trace where those two texts came from

164
00:07:05,880 --> 00:07:06,440
and send me the locations.

165
00:07:06,560 --> 00:07:07,720
We need time to prepare.

166
00:07:07,880 --> 00:07:08,400
Prepare what?

167
00:07:08,560 --> 00:07:09,760
Didn't I already bring breakfast?

168
00:07:10,080 --> 00:07:10,920
A head.

169
00:07:11,120 --> 00:07:11,640
Whose head?

170
00:07:11,720 --> 00:07:12,320
Mine.

171
00:07:12,440 --> 00:07:13,120
Yours?

172
00:07:13,280 --> 00:07:14,600
Yes. His head.

173
00:07:15,960 --> 00:07:16,880
Now I get it.

174
00:07:17,240 --> 00:07:17,880
No, you don't.

175
00:07:18,040 --> 00:07:18,800
Yes, I do.

176
00:07:18,960 --> 00:07:19,720
You're pretending.

177
00:07:19,840 --> 00:07:20,680
I really do!

178
00:07:20,800 --> 00:07:21,680
Then explain.

179
00:07:22,640 --> 00:07:24,280
Either one of you can die.

180
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:25,640
What matters

181
00:07:25,800 --> 00:07:26,840
is bringing the other's head

182
00:07:26,960 --> 00:07:27,800
back to your own organization

183
00:07:27,920 --> 00:07:29,320
as proof of loyalty.

184
00:07:29,440 --> 00:07:30,960
So now you've decided that
you're the one to die.

185
00:07:31,120 --> 00:07:32,440
Then you go meet whoever's behind this.

186
00:07:32,640 --> 00:07:34,000
They won't believe you empty-handed.

187
00:07:34,200 --> 00:07:35,600
So you bring your own body,

188
00:07:35,680 --> 00:07:36,600
your fake dead body,

189
00:07:36,880 --> 00:07:39,120
back to your organization as proof,

190
00:07:39,240 --> 00:07:39,680
right?

191
00:07:39,840 --> 00:07:41,360
Your head is your ticket in,

192
00:07:41,520 --> 00:07:42,160
isn't it?

193
00:07:42,280 --> 00:07:43,360
See? I got it.

194
00:07:47,040 --> 00:07:48,200
So that's how it works.

195
00:07:49,080 --> 00:07:50,640
Wait, that's not it?

196
00:07:51,560 --> 00:07:53,000
Is that it?

197
00:07:53,880 --> 00:07:54,760
Isn't it?

198
00:07:56,400 --> 00:07:57,960
Our conversation was all over the place,

199
00:07:57,960 --> 00:07:59,520
yet you kept track of every detail.

200
00:07:59,680 --> 00:08:02,280
None of it even connected,

201
00:08:02,280 --> 00:08:03,680
but you kept up with every jump.

202
00:08:03,800 --> 00:08:05,000
You sent me that message.

203
00:08:05,160 --> 00:08:06,040
No way! It wasn't me.

204
00:08:06,160 --> 00:08:07,640
I didn't even touch the computer.

205
00:08:07,880 --> 00:08:09,720
But your mic's been on this whole time.

206
00:08:09,920 --> 00:08:11,040
Who's listening on the other end?

207
00:08:13,280 --> 00:08:13,840
My mic?

208
00:08:14,920 --> 00:08:15,640
What mic?

209
00:08:15,760 --> 00:08:16,720
There's no mic.

210
00:08:21,240 --> 00:08:23,000
Thanks for tuning in to Nonsense Radio.

211
00:08:23,360 --> 00:08:24,320
Keeping the line open bought us time

212
00:08:24,440 --> 00:08:25,480
to track down your location.

213
00:08:25,920 --> 00:08:26,480
Get ready.

214
00:08:27,320 --> 00:08:28,480
Here comes the big bad wolf.

215
00:08:36,680 --> 00:08:38,800
We know where they are, too.

216
00:08:42,680 --> 00:08:43,640
Then let's make sure

217
00:08:45,080 --> 00:08:46,400
they die an even worse death.

218
00:09:02,200 --> 00:09:03,080
We still...

219
00:09:04,480 --> 00:09:05,440
make a pretty good team.

220
00:09:07,360 --> 00:09:08,640
We did live together for a long time.

221
00:09:11,240 --> 00:09:11,720
Lin Duo...

222
00:09:13,960 --> 00:09:14,680
I love you.

223
00:09:20,520 --> 00:09:22,440
We need to take them out fast,

224
00:09:23,320 --> 00:09:24,920
or they'll hunt us forever.

225
00:09:25,440 --> 00:09:26,320
Next time you say you love me,

226
00:09:27,200 --> 00:09:28,440
it might be at my funeral.

227
00:09:29,560 --> 00:09:30,600
Duo, watch the road.

228
00:09:39,040 --> 00:09:40,040
What have I got to be afraid of?

229
00:09:40,760 --> 00:09:41,680
Worst case, I just start over.

230
00:10:03,560 --> 00:10:05,320
Our people walked into an ambush.

231
00:10:06,120 --> 00:10:07,800
They're probably coming here now.

232
00:10:09,720 --> 00:10:11,120
Now, An...

233
00:10:12,200 --> 00:10:12,760
and...

234
00:10:14,800 --> 00:10:16,320
Both our organizations are weakened.

235
00:10:17,160 --> 00:10:18,960
We can rebuild from scratch.

236
00:10:20,200 --> 00:10:21,640
We never should've split up.

237
00:10:23,160 --> 00:10:25,320
We trained so many good people,

238
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:27,240
only to have them kill each other.

239
00:10:28,040 --> 00:10:30,120
Now we're back to training kids.

240
00:10:31,880 --> 00:10:32,640
That was...

241
00:10:33,480 --> 00:10:34,720
the Boss's plan.

242
00:10:35,400 --> 00:10:36,200
You've never met him.

243
00:10:36,200 --> 00:10:37,880
You can't grasp how he thinks.

244
00:10:40,800 --> 00:10:41,720
Now,

245
00:10:42,440 --> 00:10:45,000
only Night Owl

246
00:10:45,600 --> 00:10:47,160
and Bloody Rose remain.

247
00:10:52,240 --> 00:10:53,440
Poor kids.

248
00:10:54,440 --> 00:10:55,840
Too smart for their own good.

249
00:10:56,360 --> 00:10:57,040
Even I...

250
00:11:01,640 --> 00:11:03,400
I can't keep them under control.

251
00:11:07,760 --> 00:11:08,320
Go on.

252
00:11:11,120 --> 00:11:13,800
Will you get rid of me afterward, too?

253
00:11:15,200 --> 00:11:16,440
Of course not.

254
00:11:17,520 --> 00:11:18,640
You're so obedient

255
00:11:19,440 --> 00:11:20,400
and so dumb.

256
00:11:21,560 --> 00:11:22,800
Why would we?

257
00:11:25,360 --> 00:11:27,600
Do your job and you'll live.

258
00:11:28,320 --> 00:11:28,720
Behave.

259
00:11:37,960 --> 00:11:40,520
Don't call her dumb to her face.

260
00:11:43,720 --> 00:11:45,000
A question like that?

261
00:11:45,640 --> 00:11:47,400
That's not dumb. That's stupid.

262
00:11:48,480 --> 00:11:49,760
Then call her stupid.

263
00:11:53,080 --> 00:11:54,360
Then let's take her brain out.

264
00:12:13,960 --> 00:12:15,320
You only listen to the Boss.

265
00:12:16,120 --> 00:12:17,200
Then listen carefully.

266
00:12:25,560 --> 00:12:30,070
(Super USB Cassette Capture)

267
00:12:39,360 --> 00:12:39,960
Duo,

268
00:12:40,800 --> 00:12:42,560
can we pause the main mission

269
00:12:43,200 --> 00:12:43,920
and talk about us?

270
00:12:45,840 --> 00:12:47,120
We're just living together

271
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:48,960
and hiding who we really are.

272
00:12:49,880 --> 00:12:50,760
Once we come clean,

273
00:12:51,800 --> 00:12:53,160
apart from sleeping together,

274
00:12:54,520 --> 00:12:55,240
what else is there to talk about?

275
00:12:56,200 --> 00:12:57,080
Don't you have any...

276
00:12:57,160 --> 00:12:57,800
Of course not.

277
00:12:59,400 --> 00:13:00,200
You're just like me.

278
00:13:01,200 --> 00:13:02,720
We're both
professional clean-up killers.

279
00:13:03,440 --> 00:13:04,240
We don't do feelings.

280
00:13:05,280 --> 00:13:05,720
Right?

281
00:13:08,760 --> 00:13:09,280
No.

282
00:13:11,520 --> 00:13:12,600
When you kiss me,

283
00:13:14,160 --> 00:13:15,120
there's feeling behind it.

284
00:13:16,320 --> 00:13:17,280
I can tell the difference

285
00:13:18,800 --> 00:13:20,480
between affection and desire.

286
00:13:24,240 --> 00:13:26,040
You sound just like a naive boy.

287
00:13:27,480 --> 00:13:31,040
An inexperienced boy who got tricked
into bed by an older woman.

288
00:13:35,160 --> 00:13:35,680
Good boy.

289
00:13:37,120 --> 00:13:38,080
But I'm not making any promises.

290
00:13:58,840 --> 00:13:59,400
She did it on purpose.

291
00:14:01,640 --> 00:14:03,600
Why steal it, then leave it behind?

292
00:14:11,700 --> 00:14:14,600
(YAA D62651)

293
00:14:48,992 --> 00:14:50,200
(The Misunderstood Boy)

294
00:14:54,920 --> 00:14:55,760
You should be in the car,

295
00:14:56,320 --> 00:14:57,200
not standing here.

296
00:14:57,480 --> 00:14:57,880
You...

297
00:14:58,600 --> 00:14:59,280
Wanna dance?

298
00:15:04,920 --> 00:15:05,560
What are you doing?

299
00:15:07,480 --> 00:15:08,760
We found their location.

300
00:15:09,080 --> 00:15:09,680
But at the same time,

301
00:15:09,960 --> 00:15:11,040
they tracked us right back.

302
00:15:52,920 --> 00:15:53,920
Clever.

303
00:15:55,360 --> 00:15:56,240
Send more people.

304
00:15:56,920 --> 00:15:57,880
Search everywhere.

305
00:16:02,320 --> 00:16:02,840
Camellia.

306
00:16:03,960 --> 00:16:04,760
We've been tricked.

307
00:16:05,960 --> 00:16:07,560
We only found her tracking device.

308
00:16:08,200 --> 00:16:09,440
She's not here.

309
00:16:14,200 --> 00:16:14,680
Okay.

310
00:16:16,240 --> 00:16:17,280
Then go with Plan B.

311
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:22,280
You and An Zu go to the bunker first.

312
00:16:23,640 --> 00:16:24,640
As for Bloody Rose...

313
00:16:25,200 --> 00:16:25,920
Leave her to me.

314
00:16:27,320 --> 00:16:27,920
Don't worry.

315
00:16:29,440 --> 00:16:30,680
I'll take her out.

316
00:16:52,840 --> 00:16:54,040
The signal's blocked.

317
00:16:55,360 --> 00:16:55,960
Come on out.

318
00:17:03,120 --> 00:17:03,800
What's going on?

319
00:17:05,120 --> 00:17:06,440
Night Owl told me everything.

320
00:17:07,760 --> 00:17:08,440
Everything he said

321
00:17:09,280 --> 00:17:10,400
checked out.

322
00:17:15,200 --> 00:17:16,640
What did you tell Equinox?

323
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:17,880
How did you two meet?

324
00:17:23,760 --> 00:17:24,880
Hmm.

325
00:17:31,431 --> 00:17:34,840
(An Hour Ago)

326
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:44,560
Don't move.

327
00:17:55,650 --> 00:17:59,078
♪Does fate write every hello♪

328
00:17:59,083 --> 00:18:01,307
♪With a goodbye in mind?♪

329
00:18:07,175 --> 00:18:10,370
♪Does longing give us a beginning♪

330
00:18:10,420 --> 00:18:13,453
♪And leave us without an ending?♪

331
00:18:18,393 --> 00:18:22,793
♪I remember the way you breathe♪

332
00:18:24,273 --> 00:18:26,833
♪Countless versions of me♪

333
00:18:27,953 --> 00:18:33,673
♪All point in the same direction♪

334
00:18:34,113 --> 00:18:37,713
♪Toward you♪

335
00:18:39,703 --> 00:18:41,503
♪I'll find you♪

336
00:18:41,503 --> 00:18:44,103
♪In the silence as the world is reborn♪

337
00:18:45,063 --> 00:18:47,223
♪I'll find you♪

338
00:18:47,223 --> 00:18:49,943
♪In the instant
before anything is decided♪

339
00:18:50,743 --> 00:18:52,903
♪I'll find you♪

340
00:18:52,903 --> 00:18:55,583
♪In the gaps
where time overlaps and slips♪

341
00:18:56,463 --> 00:18:58,343
♪I'll find you♪

342
00:19:02,543 --> 00:19:04,143
♪I'll find you♪

343
00:19:04,463 --> 00:19:07,103
♪In the promises left unsaid♪

344
00:19:07,903 --> 00:19:09,823
♪I'll find you♪

345
00:19:10,023 --> 00:19:12,743
♪In every pause between heartbeats♪

346
00:19:13,543 --> 00:19:15,543
♪I'll find you♪

347
00:19:15,703 --> 00:19:18,303
♪Where the last faint light fades♪

348
00:19:19,343 --> 00:19:21,663
♪I'll find you♪

349
00:19:25,023 --> 00:19:30,903
♪I'll find you♪
